message: "If you use MechAudit in research, please cite the software and record the exact version and numerical tolerances."
title: "MechAudit: finite mechanism design and optimal-constraint analysis"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Staffini"
    given-names: "Alessio"
    affiliation: "Studio Strata, Tokyo, Japan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5001-349X"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-22
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23540591
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/studio-strata/mechaudit"
url: "https://studio-strata.github.io/mechaudit/"
abstract: >-
  MechAudit is a Python research workbench for auditing finite direct mechanisms,
  designing randomized mechanisms with sparse linear programming, and studying
  constraint activity across near-optimal faces.
keywords:
  - mechanism design
  - incentive compatibility
  - linear programming
  - computational economics
  - numerical diagnostics
